      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum prescribed adult dose of 3,200 mg/day. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nTypical oral adult dosing is:\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n- **Anti-inflammatory or arthritis dosing:** 400\u2013800 mg three or four times daily. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and the lowest effective dose is preferred.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Something else\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency, ideally with your resident or attending, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
